      "back": "**Pattern:** HashSet\\n\\n**Key insight:** Insert each value into a set; if insertion fails, you've seen it before.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean containsDuplicate(int[] nums) {\\n        Set<Integer> seen = new HashSet<>();\\n        for (int x : nums) if (!seen.add(x)) return true;\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def containsDuplicate(self, nums: List[int]) -> bool:\\n        seen = set()\\n        for x in nums:\\n            if x in seen:\\n                return True\\n            seen.add(x)\\n        return False\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Sorting also works in O(n log n) but mutates the input.",
