      "front": "**Valid Anagram** · Easy\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-anagram/)\\n\\nDecide whether two lowercase strings use exactly the same letters with the same counts.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Frequency count\\n\\n**Key insight:** Count up for one string, down for the other; all counters must end at zero.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean isAnagram(String s, String t) {\\n        if (s.length() != t.length()) return false;\\n        int[] cnt = new int[26];\\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\\n            cnt[s.charAt(i) - 'a']++;\\n            cnt[t.charAt(i) - 'a']--;\\n        }\\n        for (int c : cnt) if (c != 0) return false;\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def isAnagram(self, s: str, t: str) -> bool:\\n        if len(s) != len(t):\\n            return False\\n        cnt = [0] * 26\\n        for a, b in zip(s, t):\\n            cnt[ord(a) - ord('a')] += 1\\n            cnt[ord(b) - ord('a')] -= 1\\n        return all(c == 0 for c in cnt)\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Skip the length check and strings of different lengths would need extra handling in the counter loop.",
