      "front": "**Two Sum** · Easy\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/two-sum/)\\n\\nReturn the indices of the two entries that add up to a target.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** HashMap complement\\n\\n**Key insight:** While scanning, look up target - x among values already seen.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int[] twoSum(int[] nums, int target) {\\n        Map<Integer, Integer> idx = new HashMap<>();\\n        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\\n            Integer j = idx.get(target - nums[i]);\\n            if (j != null) return new int[]{j, i};\\n            idx.put(nums[i], i);\\n        }\\n        return new int[0];\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def twoSum(self, nums: List[int], target: int) -> List[int]:\\n        idx = {}\\n        for i, x in enumerate(nums):\\n            if target - x in idx:\\n                return [idx[target - x], i]\\n            idx[x] = i\\n        return []\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Look up before inserting, or x + x = target will pair an element with itself.",
