      "id": "nc150-top-k-frequent-elements",
      "front": "**Top K Frequent Elements** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/top-k-frequent-elements/)\\n\\nReturn the k values that occur most often in an array.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Counting + bucket sort\\n\\n**Key insight:** Frequencies are bounded by n, so bucket values by count and read buckets from high to low.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int[] topKFrequent(int[] nums, int k) {\\n        Map<Integer, Integer> freq = new HashMap<>();\\n        for (int x : nums) freq.merge(x, 1, Integer::sum);\\n        List<Integer>[] buckets = new List[nums.length + 1];\\n        for (var e : freq.entrySet()) {\\n            int f = e.getValue();\\n            if (buckets[f] == null) buckets[f] = new ArrayList<>();\\n            buckets[f].add(e.getKey());\\n        }\\n        int[] res = new int[k];\\n        int i = 0;\\n        for (int f = nums.length; f > 0 && i < k; f--)\\n            if (buckets[f] != null)\\n                for (int v : buckets[f]) if (i < k) res[i++] = v;\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom collections import Counter\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def topKFrequent(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> List[int]:\\n        buckets = [[] for _ in range(len(nums) + 1)]\\n        for v, f in Counter(nums).items():\\n            buckets[f].append(v)\\n        res = []\\n        for f in range(len(nums), 0, -1):\\n            for v in buckets[f]:\\n                if len(res) == k:\\n                    return res\\n                res.append(v)\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Bucket array needs size n + 1 since a value can appear n times.",
