      "back": "**Pattern:** HashSet + sequence starts\\n\\n**Key insight:** Only start counting from x when x-1 is absent; each number is then visited O(1) times.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int longestConsecutive(int[] nums) {\\n        Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();\\n        for (int x : nums) set.add(x);\\n        int best = 0;\\n        for (int x : set) {\\n            if (set.contains(x - 1)) continue;\\n            int len = 1;\\n            while (set.contains(x + len)) len++;\\n            best = Math.max(best, len);\\n        }\\n        return best;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def longestConsecutive(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\\n        s = set(nums)\\n        best = 0\\n        for x in s:\\n            if x - 1 in s:\\n                continue\\n            length = 1\\n            while x + length in s:\\n                length += 1\\n            best = max(best, length)\\n        return best\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Iterate the set, not the array — duplicates in the array can make it quadratic.",
