      "front": "**Valid Palindrome** · Easy\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-palindrome/)\\n\\nIgnoring case and anything that isn't a letter or digit, decide whether a string reads the same both ways.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Two pointers from both ends\\n\\n**Key insight:** Skip non-alphanumerics on each side, compare lowercase chars, move inward.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean isPalindrome(String s) {\\n        int l = 0, r = s.length() - 1;\\n        while (l < r) {\\n            if (!Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(l))) l++;\\n            else if (!Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(r))) r--;\\n            else if (Character.toLowerCase(s.charAt(l++)) != Character.toLowerCase(s.charAt(r--))) return false;\\n        }\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def isPalindrome(self, s: str) -> bool:\\n        l, r = 0, len(s) - 1\\n        while l < r:\\n            if not s[l].isalnum():\\n                l += 1\\n            elif not s[r].isalnum():\\n                r -= 1\\n            elif s[l].lower() != s[r].lower():\\n                return False\\n            else:\\n                l += 1\\n                r -= 1\\n        return True\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Digits count as alphanumeric — '0P' is not a palindrome.",
