      "front": "**Two Sum II - Input Array Is Sorted** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/two-sum-ii-input-array-is-sorted/)\\n\\nIn a sorted array, return the 1-based positions of two numbers that sum to a target using constant extra space.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Converging two pointers\\n\\n**Key insight:** Sum too small → move left up; too big → move right down.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int[] twoSum(int[] numbers, int target) {\\n        int l = 0, r = numbers.length - 1;\\n        while (l < r) {\\n            int sum = numbers[l] + numbers[r];\\n            if (sum == target) return new int[]{l + 1, r + 1};\\n            if (sum < target) l++; else r--;\\n        }\\n        return new int[0];\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def twoSum(self, numbers: List[int], target: int) -> List[int]:\\n        l, r = 0, len(numbers) - 1\\n        while l < r:\\n            s = numbers[l] + numbers[r]\\n            if s == target:\\n                return [l + 1, r + 1]\\n            if s < target:\\n                l += 1\\n            else:\\n                r -= 1\\n        return []\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Answer is 1-indexed.",
