      "id": "nc150-3sum",
      "front": "**3Sum** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/3sum/)\\n\\nList every distinct triple of values in an array that sums to zero.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Sort + fix one + two pointers\\n\\n**Key insight:** Sort, fix nums[i], then two-pointer the rest for -nums[i]; skip equal neighbors to dedupe.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public List<List<Integer>> threeSum(int[] nums) {\\n        Arrays.sort(nums);\\n        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();\\n        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length - 2 && nums[i] <= 0; i++) {\\n            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;\\n            int l = i + 1, r = nums.length - 1;\\n            while (l < r) {\\n                int s = nums[i] + nums[l] + nums[r];\\n                if (s < 0) l++;\\n                else if (s > 0) r--;\\n                else {\\n                    res.add(List.of(nums[i], nums[l], nums[r]));\\n                    while (l < r && nums[l] == nums[l + 1]) l++;\\n                    l++; r--;\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def threeSum(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\\n        nums.sort()\\n        res = []\\n        for i in range(len(nums) - 2):\\n            if nums[i] > 0:\\n                break\\n            if i > 0 and nums[i] == nums[i - 1]:\\n                continue\\n            l, r = i + 1, len(nums) - 1\\n            while l < r:\\n                s = nums[i] + nums[l] + nums[r]\\n                if s < 0:\\n                    l += 1\\n                elif s > 0:\\n                    r -= 1\\n                else:\\n                    res.append([nums[i], nums[l], nums[r]])\\n                    while l < r and nums[l] == nums[l + 1]:\\n                        l += 1\\n                    l += 1\\n                    r -= 1\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n²) / O(1) extra (ignoring sort)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Forgetting to skip duplicates for both i and l yields repeated triples.",
