      "id": "nc150-container-with-most-water",
      "front": "**Container With Most Water** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/container-with-most-water/)\\n\\nPick two vertical lines that, together with the x-axis, hold the most water.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Converging two pointers\\n\\n**Key insight:** Area is limited by the shorter line, so moving the taller one can never help — move the shorter.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int maxArea(int[] height) {\\n        int l = 0, r = height.length - 1, best = 0;\\n        while (l < r) {\\n            best = Math.max(best, Math.min(height[l], height[r]) * (r - l));\\n            if (height[l] < height[r]) l++; else r--;\\n        }\\n        return best;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def maxArea(self, height: List[int]) -> int:\\n        l, r, best = 0, len(height) - 1, 0\\n        while l < r:\\n            best = max(best, min(height[l], height[r]) * (r - l))\\n            if height[l] < height[r]:\\n                l += 1\\n            else:\\n                r -= 1\\n        return best\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Don't confuse with Trapping Rain Water — here only two lines matter.",
