      "id": "nc150-trapping-rain-water",
      "front": "**Trapping Rain Water** · Hard\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/trapping-rain-water/)\\n\\nGiven bar heights, compute how much rain gets trapped between the bars.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Two pointers with running maxes\\n\\n**Key insight:** Water at i = min(maxLeft, maxRight) - h[i]; process the side with the smaller max, since that bound is final.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int trap(int[] height) {\\n        int l = 0, r = height.length - 1, lMax = 0, rMax = 0, water = 0;\\n        while (l < r) {\\n            if (height[l] < height[r]) {\\n                lMax = Math.max(lMax, height[l]);\\n                water += lMax - height[l++];\\n            } else {\\n                rMax = Math.max(rMax, height[r]);\\n                water += rMax - height[r--];\\n            }\\n        }\\n        return water;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def trap(self, height: List[int]) -> int:\\n        l, r = 0, len(height) - 1\\n        l_max = r_max = water = 0\\n        while l < r:\\n            if height[l] < height[r]:\\n                l_max = max(l_max, height[l])\\n                water += l_max - height[l]\\n                l += 1\\n            else:\\n                r_max = max(r_max, height[r])\\n                water += r_max - height[r]\\n                r -= 1\\n        return water\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Update the max before adding water so the result never goes negative.",
