      "id": "nc150-longest-repeating-character-replacement",
      "front": "**Longest Repeating Character Replacement** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-repeating-character-replacement/)\\n\\nWith at most k letter changes allowed, find the longest substring that can be turned into one repeated letter.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Variable sliding window + counts\\n\\n**Key insight:** Window is valid while length - maxFreq <= k; maxFreq never needs to decrease.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int characterReplacement(String s, int k) {\\n        int[] cnt = new int[26];\\n        int left = 0, maxF = 0, best = 0;\\n        for (int r = 0; r < s.length(); r++) {\\n            maxF = Math.max(maxF, ++cnt[s.charAt(r) - 'A']);\\n            while (r - left + 1 - maxF > k) cnt[s.charAt(left++) - 'A']--;\\n            best = Math.max(best, r - left + 1);\\n        }\\n        return best;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def characterReplacement(self, s: str, k: int) -> int:\\n        cnt = [0] * 26\\n        left = max_f = best = 0\\n        for r, ch in enumerate(s):\\n            cnt[ord(ch) - ord('A')] += 1\\n            max_f = max(max_f, cnt[ord(ch) - ord('A')])\\n            while r - left + 1 - max_f > k:\\n                cnt[ord(s[left]) - ord('A')] -= 1\\n                left += 1\\n            best = max(best, r - left + 1)\\n        return best\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(26)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Input is uppercase — index with 'A', not 'a'.",
