      "id": "nc150-permutation-in-string",
      "front": "**Permutation in String** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/permutation-in-string/)\\n\\nDecide whether some rearrangement of s1 appears as a contiguous piece of s2.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Fixed-size sliding window + counts\\n\\n**Key insight:** Slide a window of |s1| over s2 and compare 26-letter counts.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean checkInclusion(String s1, String s2) {\\n        if (s1.length() > s2.length()) return false;\\n        int[] need = new int[26], win = new int[26];\\n        for (char c : s1.toCharArray()) need[c - 'a']++;\\n        for (int i = 0; i < s2.length(); i++) {\\n            win[s2.charAt(i) - 'a']++;\\n            if (i >= s1.length()) win[s2.charAt(i - s1.length()) - 'a']--;\\n            if (Arrays.equals(need, win)) return true;\\n        }\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def checkInclusion(self, s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:\\n        m = len(s1)\\n        if m > len(s2):\\n            return False\\n        need, win = [0] * 26, [0] * 26\\n        for c in s1:\\n            need[ord(c) - ord('a')] += 1\\n        for i, c in enumerate(s2):\\n            win[ord(c) - ord('a')] += 1\\n            if i >= m:\\n                win[ord(s2[i - m]) - ord('a')] -= 1\\n            if need == win:\\n                return True\\n        return False\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(26·n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Return early when s1 is longer than s2.",
