      "id": "nc150-valid-parentheses",
      "front": "**Valid Parentheses** · Easy\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-parentheses/)\\n\\nCheck that every bracket in a string of ()[]{} is closed by the right type in the right order.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Stack\\n\\n**Key insight:** Push the expected closer for each opener; each closer must match the top.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean isValid(String s) {\\n        Deque<Character> st = new ArrayDeque<>();\\n        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {\\n            if (c == '(') st.push(')');\\n            else if (c == '[') st.push(']');\\n            else if (c == '{') st.push('}');\\n            else if (st.isEmpty() || st.pop() != c) return false;\\n        }\\n        return st.isEmpty();\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def isValid(self, s: str) -> bool:\\n        pairs = {'(': ')', '[': ']', '{': '}'}\\n        st = []\\n        for c in s:\\n            if c in pairs:\\n                st.append(pairs[c])\\n            elif not st or st.pop() != c:\\n                return False\\n        return not st\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Leftover openers mean invalid — check the stack is empty at the end.",
