      "id": "nc150-min-stack",
      "front": "**Min Stack** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/min-stack/)\\n\\nBuild a stack that also returns its current minimum in constant time.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Stack of (value, min) pairs\\n\\n**Key insight:** Store alongside each value the minimum at the time it was pushed.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass MinStack {\\n    private final Deque<int[]> st = new ArrayDeque<>();\\n    public MinStack() {}\\n    public void push(int val) {\\n        int min = st.isEmpty() ? val : Math.min(val, st.peek()[1]);\\n        st.push(new int[]{val, min});\\n    }\\n    public void pop() { st.pop(); }\\n    public int top() { return st.peek()[0]; }\\n    public int getMin() { return st.peek()[1]; }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass MinStack:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.st = []  # (val, min so far)\\n\\n    def push(self, val: int) -> None:\\n        cur_min = val if not self.st else min(val, self.st[-1][1])\\n        self.st.append((val, cur_min))\\n\\n    def pop(self) -> None:\\n        self.st.pop()\\n\\n    def top(self) -> int:\\n        return self.st[-1][0]\\n\\n    def getMin(self) -> int:\\n        return self.st[-1][1]\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(1) per op / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** A single min variable can't recover the previous min after a pop.",
