      "id": "nc150-daily-temperatures",
      "front": "**Daily Temperatures** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/daily-temperatures/)\\n\\nFor each day, say how many days until a strictly warmer one (0 if never).\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Monotonic decreasing stack\\n\\n**Key insight:** Keep indices of unresolved days; a warmer day pops and answers them.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int[] dailyTemperatures(int[] temps) {\\n        int[] res = new int[temps.length];\\n        Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();\\n        for (int i = 0; i < temps.length; i++) {\\n            while (!st.isEmpty() && temps[st.peek()] < temps[i]) {\\n                int j = st.pop();\\n                res[j] = i - j;\\n            }\\n            st.push(i);\\n        }\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def dailyTemperatures(self, temperatures: List[int]) -> List[int]:\\n        res = [0] * len(temperatures)\\n        st = []\\n        for i, t in enumerate(temperatures):\\n            while st and temperatures[st[-1]] < t:\\n                j = st.pop()\\n                res[j] = i - j\\n            st.append(i)\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Use strict < — equal temperatures are not warmer.",
