      "id": "nc150-largest-rectangle-in-histogram",
      "front": "**Largest Rectangle in Histogram** · Hard\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/largest-rectangle-in-histogram/)\\n\\nFind the largest rectangle area that fits under a bar chart.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Monotonic increasing stack\\n\\n**Key insight:** When a shorter bar arrives, popped bars can't extend further right; their width spans from the new top+1 to i-1.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int largestRectangleArea(int[] heights) {\\n        Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();\\n        int best = 0, n = heights.length;\\n        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\\n            int h = i == n ? 0 : heights[i];\\n            while (!st.isEmpty() && heights[st.peek()] >= h) {\\n                int height = heights[st.pop()];\\n                int left = st.isEmpty() ? -1 : st.peek();\\n                best = Math.max(best, height * (i - left - 1));\\n            }\\n            st.push(i);\\n        }\\n        return best;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def largestRectangleArea(self, heights: List[int]) -> int:\\n        st, best, n = [], 0, len(heights)\\n        for i in range(n + 1):\\n            h = 0 if i == n else heights[i]\\n            while st and heights[st[-1]] >= h:\\n                height = heights[st.pop()]\\n                left = st[-1] if st else -1\\n                best = max(best, height * (i - left - 1))\\n            st.append(i)\\n        return best\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Add a sentinel 0 at the end to flush the stack.",
