      "id": "nc150-binary-tree-right-side-view",
      "front": "**Binary Tree Right Side View** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/binary-tree-right-side-view/)\\n\\nList the values you would see looking at the tree from its right side, top to bottom.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** BFS by level (or right-first DFS)\\n\\n**Key insight:** The last node popped in each BFS level is the one visible from the right.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public List<Integer> rightSideView(TreeNode root) {\\n        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();\\n        Deque<TreeNode> q = new ArrayDeque<>();\\n        if (root != null) q.add(root);\\n        while (!q.isEmpty()) {\\n            int size = q.size();\\n            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\\n                TreeNode n = q.poll();\\n                if (i == size - 1) res.add(n.val);\\n                if (n.left != null) q.add(n.left);\\n                if (n.right != null) q.add(n.right);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom collections import deque\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def rightSideView(self, root: Optional[TreeNode]) -> List[int]:\\n        res = []\\n        q = deque([root] if root else [])\\n        while q:\\n            size = len(q)\\n            for i in range(size):\\n                n = q.popleft()\\n                if i == size - 1:\\n                    res.append(n.val)\\n                if n.left:\\n                    q.append(n.left)\\n                if n.right:\\n                    q.append(n.right)\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(w)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Only following right children misses left nodes that stick out deeper.",
