      "back": "**Pattern:** Min-heap of size k (or Quickselect)\\n\\n**Key insight:** After streaming all values through a size-k min-heap, the top is the k-th largest.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int findKthLargest(int[] nums, int k) {\\n        PriorityQueue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();\\n        for (int x : nums) {\\n            pq.offer(x);\\n            if (pq.size() > k) pq.poll();\\n        }\\n        return pq.peek();\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nimport heapq\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def findKthLargest(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\\n        pq = []\\n        for x in nums:\\n            heapq.heappush(pq, x)\\n            if len(pq) > k:\\n                heapq.heappop(pq)\\n        return pq[0]\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n log k) / O(k)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Deduplicating values — the k-th largest counts duplicates separately.",
