      "id": "nc150-subsets-ii",
      "front": "**Subsets II** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/subsets-ii/)\\n\\nReturn all distinct subsets of an array that may contain duplicates.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Backtracking with duplicate skipping\\n\\n**Key insight:** Sort first; at each depth only branch on the first of a run of equal values.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public List<List<Integer>> subsetsWithDup(int[] nums) {\\n        Arrays.sort(nums);\\n        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();\\n        go(nums, 0, new ArrayList<>(), res);\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n    private void go(int[] nums, int start, List<Integer> path, List<List<Integer>> res) {\\n        res.add(new ArrayList<>(path));\\n        for (int i = start; i < nums.length; i++) {\\n            if (i > start && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;\\n            path.add(nums[i]);\\n            go(nums, i + 1, path, res);\\n            path.remove(path.size() - 1);\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def subsetsWithDup(self, nums: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\\n        nums = sorted(nums)\\n        res, path = [], []\\n\\n        def go(start: int) -> None:\\n            res.append(path[:])\\n            for i in range(start, len(nums)):\\n                if i > start and nums[i] == nums[i - 1]:\\n                    continue\\n                path.append(nums[i])\\n                go(i + 1)\\n                path.pop()\\n\\n        go(0)\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n·2ⁿ) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Skipping duplicates without sorting first leaves non-adjacent duplicates undetected.",
