      "id": "nc150-swim-in-rising-water",
      "front": "**Swim in Rising Water** · Hard\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/swim-in-rising-water/)\\n\\nIn an n×n elevation grid, find the minimum time t such that you can go from top-left to bottom-right only through cells with elevation ≤ t.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Minimax path (Dijkstra on max-edge)\\n\\n**Key insight:** Path cost is the maximum cell on it; a min-heap keyed on that max finalizes cells in order.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int swimInWater(int[][] grid) {\\n        int n = grid.length;\\n        boolean[][] seen = new boolean[n][n];\\n        PriorityQueue<int[]> pq = new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> a[0] - b[0]);\\n        pq.add(new int[]{grid[0][0], 0, 0});\\n        seen[0][0] = true;\\n        int[] d = {0, 1, 0, -1, 0};\\n        while (true) {\\n            int[] c = pq.poll();\\n            if (c[1] == n - 1 && c[2] == n - 1) return c[0];\\n            for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n                int r = c[1] + d[i], col = c[2] + d[i + 1];\\n                if (r < 0 || col < 0 || r >= n || col >= n || seen[r][col]) continue;\\n                seen[r][col] = true;\\n                pq.add(new int[]{Math.max(c[0], grid[r][col]), r, col});\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nimport heapq\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def swimInWater(self, grid: List[List[int]]) -> int:\\n        n = len(grid)\\n        seen = {(0, 0)}\\n        pq = [(grid[0][0], 0, 0)]\\n        while True:\\n            t, r, c = heapq.heappop(pq)\\n            if r == n - 1 and c == n - 1:\\n                return t\\n            for nr, nc in ((r + 1, c), (r - 1, c), (r, c + 1), (r, c - 1)):\\n                if 0 <= nr < n and 0 <= nc < n and (nr, nc) not in seen:\\n                    seen.add((nr, nc))\\n                    heapq.heappush(pq, (max(t, grid[nr][nc]), nr, nc))\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n² log n) / O(n²)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Starting cell's own height counts — don't initialize the cost to 0.",
