      "id": "nc150-min-cost-climbing-stairs",
      "front": "**Min Cost Climbing Stairs** · Easy\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/min-cost-climbing-stairs/)\\n\\nEach step has a cost paid when you stand on it; starting at step 0 or 1 and moving 1 or 2 at a time, find the minimum cost to get past the top.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Linear DP\\n\\n**Key insight:** best(i) = cost[i] + min(best(i-1), best(i-2)); answer is min of the last two.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int minCostClimbingStairs(int[] cost) {\\n        int a = 0, b = 0;\\n        for (int i = 2; i <= cost.length; i++) {\\n            int c = Math.min(b + cost[i - 1], a + cost[i - 2]);\\n            a = b; b = c;\\n        }\\n        return b;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def minCostClimbingStairs(self, cost: List[int]) -> int:\\n        a = b = 0\\n        for i in range(2, len(cost) + 1):\\n            a, b = b, min(b + cost[i - 1], a + cost[i - 2])\\n        return b\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** The top is one past the last index — don't return the cost of landing on the last step.",
