      "front": "**House Robber** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/house-robber/)\\n\\nPick a subset of houses with no two adjacent to maximize money stolen.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Linear DP (take / skip)\\n\\n**Key insight:** best(i) = max(best(i-1), best(i-2) + nums[i]).\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int rob(int[] nums) {\\n        int prev = 0, cur = 0;\\n        for (int x : nums) { int t = Math.max(cur, prev + x); prev = cur; cur = t; }\\n        return cur;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def rob(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\\n        prev = cur = 0\\n        for x in nums:\\n            prev, cur = cur, max(cur, prev + x)\\n        return cur\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Greedy alternating (evens vs odds) fails, e.g. [2,1,1,2].",
