      "id": "nc150-house-robber-ii",
      "front": "**House Robber II** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/house-robber-ii/)\\n\\nSame as House Robber but houses form a circle, so the first and last are adjacent.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Linear DP run twice\\n\\n**Key insight:** Either skip the first house or skip the last; take the better of two linear robs.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int rob(int[] nums) {\\n        if (nums.length == 1) return nums[0];\\n        return Math.max(line(nums, 0, nums.length - 2), line(nums, 1, nums.length - 1));\\n    }\\n    int line(int[] a, int lo, int hi) {\\n        int prev = 0, cur = 0;\\n        for (int i = lo; i <= hi; i++) { int t = Math.max(cur, prev + a[i]); prev = cur; cur = t; }\\n        return cur;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def rob(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\\n        if len(nums) == 1:\\n            return nums[0]\\n\\n        def line(a: List[int]) -> int:\\n            prev = cur = 0\\n            for x in a:\\n                prev, cur = cur, max(cur, prev + x)\\n            return cur\\n\\n        return max(line(nums[:-1]), line(nums[1:]))\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Single-house input: both ranges become empty unless handled.",
