      "id": "nc150-longest-palindromic-substring",
      "front": "**Longest Palindromic Substring** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-palindromic-substring/)\\n\\nReturn the longest contiguous substring that reads the same both ways.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Expand around center\\n\\n**Key insight:** Each palindrome has a center (2n-1 of them); expand outward while ends match.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    int start = 0, len = 0;\\n    public String longestPalindrome(String s) {\\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) { grow(s, i, i); grow(s, i, i + 1); }\\n        return s.substring(start, start + len);\\n    }\\n    void grow(String s, int l, int r) {\\n        while (l >= 0 && r < s.length() && s.charAt(l) == s.charAt(r)) { l--; r++; }\\n        if (r - l - 1 > len) { len = r - l - 1; start = l + 1; }\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def longestPalindrome(self, s: str) -> str:\\n        start = length = 0\\n\\n        def grow(l: int, r: int) -> None:\\n            nonlocal start, length\\n            while l >= 0 and r < len(s) and s[l] == s[r]:\\n                l -= 1\\n                r += 1\\n            if r - l - 1 > length:\\n                start, length = l + 1, r - l - 1\\n\\n        for i in range(len(s)):\\n            grow(i, i)\\n            grow(i, i + 1)\\n        return s[start:start + length]\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n²) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Forgetting even-length centers (between two chars).",
