      "id": "nc150-palindromic-substrings",
      "front": "**Palindromic Substrings** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/palindromic-substrings/)\\n\\nCount all substrings (by position) that are palindromes.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Expand around center\\n\\n**Key insight:** Every successful expansion step is one more palindrome.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int countSubstrings(String s) {\\n        int count = 0;\\n        for (int c = 0; c < 2 * s.length() - 1; c++) {\\n            int l = c / 2, r = l + c % 2;\\n            while (l >= 0 && r < s.length() && s.charAt(l) == s.charAt(r)) { count++; l--; r++; }\\n        }\\n        return count;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def countSubstrings(self, s: str) -> int:\\n        count = 0\\n        for c in range(2 * len(s) - 1):\\n            l, r = c // 2, c // 2 + c % 2\\n            while l >= 0 and r < len(s) and s[l] == s[r]:\\n                count += 1\\n                l -= 1\\n                r += 1\\n        return count\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n²) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Identical substrings at different positions count separately.",
