      "id": "nc150-coin-change",
      "front": "**Coin Change** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/coin-change/)\\n\\nFind the fewest coins (unlimited supply) summing to an amount, or -1.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Unbounded knapsack (min)\\n\\n**Key insight:** dp[a] = 1 + min over coins c of dp[a-c].\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int coinChange(int[] coins, int amount) {\\n        int[] dp = new int[amount + 1];\\n        Arrays.fill(dp, amount + 1);\\n        dp[0] = 0;\\n        for (int a = 1; a <= amount; a++)\\n            for (int c : coins)\\n                if (c <= a) dp[a] = Math.min(dp[a], dp[a - c] + 1);\\n        return dp[amount] > amount ? -1 : dp[amount];\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def coinChange(self, coins: List[int], amount: int) -> int:\\n        dp = [0] + [amount + 1] * amount\\n        for a in range(1, amount + 1):\\n            for c in coins:\\n                if c <= a:\\n                    dp[a] = min(dp[a], dp[a - c] + 1)\\n        return -1 if dp[amount] > amount else dp[amount]\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(amount · coins) / O(amount)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Greedy largest-coin-first is wrong for coin sets like [1,3,4], amount 6.",
