      "id": "nc150-coin-change-ii",
      "front": "**Coin Change II** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/coin-change-ii/)\\n\\nCount the combinations (order-insensitive) of coins that sum to an amount.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Unbounded knapsack (count)\\n\\n**Key insight:** Loop coins outside, amounts inside, so each combination is counted once.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int change(int amount, int[] coins) {\\n        int[] ways = new int[amount + 1];\\n        ways[0] = 1;\\n        for (int c : coins)\\n            for (int a = c; a <= amount; a++) ways[a] += ways[a - c];\\n        return ways[amount];\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def change(self, amount: int, coins: List[int]) -> int:\\n        ways = [1] + [0] * amount\\n        for c in coins:\\n            for a in range(c, amount + 1):\\n                ways[a] += ways[a - c]\\n        return ways[amount]\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(amount · coins) / O(amount)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Swapping the loops counts permutations instead of combinations.",
