      "id": "nc150-interleaving-string",
      "front": "**Interleaving String** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/interleaving-string/)\\n\\nDecide whether s3 is formed by interleaving s1 and s2 while keeping each one's character order.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Two-string DP\\n\\n**Key insight:** ok[i][j]: first i of s1 and j of s2 form the first i+j of s3; extend from the left or top cell.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean isInterleave(String a, String b, String c) {\\n        if (a.length() + b.length() != c.length()) return false;\\n        boolean[] ok = new boolean[b.length() + 1];\\n        for (int i = 0; i <= a.length(); i++)\\n            for (int j = 0; j <= b.length(); j++) {\\n                if (i == 0 && j == 0) { ok[0] = true; continue; }\\n                char t = c.charAt(i + j - 1);\\n                boolean fromA = i > 0 && ok[j] && a.charAt(i - 1) == t;\\n                boolean fromB = j > 0 && ok[j - 1] && b.charAt(j - 1) == t;\\n                ok[j] = fromA || fromB;\\n            }\\n        return ok[b.length()];\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def isInterleave(self, s1: str, s2: str, s3: str) -> bool:\\n        if len(s1) + len(s2) != len(s3):\\n            return False\\n        ok = [False] * (len(s2) + 1)\\n        for i in range(len(s1) + 1):\\n            for j in range(len(s2) + 1):\\n                if i == 0 and j == 0:\\n                    ok[0] = True\\n                    continue\\n                t = s3[i + j - 1]\\n                from_a = i > 0 and ok[j] and s1[i - 1] == t\\n                from_b = j > 0 and ok[j - 1] and s2[j - 1] == t\\n                ok[j] = from_a or from_b\\n        return ok[-1]\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(m·n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Check the length sum first, or indexing c goes out of bounds.",
