      "id": "nc150-distinct-subsequences",
      "front": "**Distinct Subsequences** · Hard\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/distinct-subsequences/)\\n\\nCount how many distinct subsequences of s equal t.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Two-string counting DP\\n\\n**Key insight:** For each char of s, update counts for t positions right-to-left: if chars match, add the count of the shorter prefix.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int numDistinct(String s, String t) {\\n        long[] dp = new long[t.length() + 1];\\n        dp[0] = 1;\\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++)\\n            for (int j = t.length(); j >= 1; j--)\\n                if (s.charAt(i) == t.charAt(j - 1)) dp[j] += dp[j - 1];\\n        return (int) dp[t.length()];\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def numDistinct(self, s: str, t: str) -> int:\\n        dp = [1] + [0] * len(t)\\n        for ch in s:\\n            for j in range(len(t), 0, -1):\\n                if ch == t[j - 1]:\\n                    dp[j] += dp[j - 1]\\n        return dp[-1]\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(m·n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Iterating j left-to-right reuses the same s character twice.",
