      "id": "nc150-jump-game",
      "front": "**Jump Game** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/jump-game/)\\n\\nEach value is a max jump length; decide whether you can reach the last index from the first.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Greedy reach\\n\\n**Key insight:** Track the farthest reachable index; fail if you ever stand beyond it.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean canJump(int[] nums) {\\n        int reach = 0;\\n        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\\n            if (i > reach) return false;\\n            reach = Math.max(reach, i + nums[i]);\\n        }\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def canJump(self, nums: List[int]) -> bool:\\n        reach = 0\\n        for i, x in enumerate(nums):\\n            if i > reach:\\n                return False\\n            reach = max(reach, i + x)\\n        return True\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Zeros are only fatal if no earlier index can jump over them.",
