      "id": "nc150-spiral-matrix",
      "front": "**Spiral Matrix** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/spiral-matrix/)\\n\\nReturn all elements of a matrix in clockwise spiral order.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Shrinking boundaries\\n\\n**Key insight:** Walk top row, right column, bottom row, left column, then shrink; guard the last two for single rows/cols.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public List<Integer> spiralOrder(int[][] m) {\\n        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();\\n        int top = 0, bot = m.length - 1, left = 0, right = m[0].length - 1;\\n        while (top <= bot && left <= right) {\\n            for (int c = left; c <= right; c++) res.add(m[top][c]);\\n            for (int r = top + 1; r <= bot; r++) res.add(m[r][right]);\\n            if (top < bot) for (int c = right - 1; c >= left; c--) res.add(m[bot][c]);\\n            if (left < right) for (int r = bot - 1; r > top; r--) res.add(m[r][left]);\\n            top++; bot--; left++; right--;\\n        }\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def spiralOrder(self, matrix: List[List[int]]) -> List[int]:\\n        res = []\\n        top, bot, left, right = 0, len(matrix) - 1, 0, len(matrix[0]) - 1\\n        while top <= bot and left <= right:\\n            res.extend(matrix[top][c] for c in range(left, right + 1))\\n            res.extend(matrix[r][right] for r in range(top + 1, bot + 1))\\n            if top < bot:\\n                res.extend(matrix[bot][c] for c in range(right - 1, left - 1, -1))\\n            if left < right:\\n                res.extend(matrix[r][left] for r in range(bot - 1, top, -1))\\n            top, bot, left, right = top + 1, bot - 1, left + 1, right - 1\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(m·n) / O(1) extra\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Without the top<bot / left<right guards, a middle row or column gets added twice.",
