      "id": "nc150-set-matrix-zeroes",
      "front": "**Set Matrix Zeroes** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/set-matrix-zeroes/)\\n\\nIf a cell is 0, zero its entire row and column, in place.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Use first row/column as markers\\n\\n**Key insight:** Record zero rows/cols in row 0 and col 0; track col 0's own state in a flag.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public void setZeroes(int[][] m) {\\n        int R = m.length, C = m[0].length;\\n        boolean col0 = false;\\n        for (int r = 0; r < R; r++) {\\n            if (m[r][0] == 0) col0 = true;\\n            for (int c = 1; c < C; c++)\\n                if (m[r][c] == 0) { m[r][0] = 0; m[0][c] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        for (int r = R - 1; r >= 0; r--) {\\n            for (int c = C - 1; c >= 1; c--)\\n                if (m[r][0] == 0 || m[0][c] == 0) m[r][c] = 0;\\n            if (col0) m[r][0] = 0;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def setZeroes(self, matrix: List[List[int]]) -> None:\\n        R, C = len(matrix), len(matrix[0])\\n        col0 = False\\n        for r in range(R):\\n            if matrix[r][0] == 0:\\n                col0 = True\\n            for c in range(1, C):\\n                if matrix[r][c] == 0:\\n                    matrix[r][0] = matrix[0][c] = 0\\n        for r in range(R - 1, -1, -1):\\n            for c in range(C - 1, 0, -1):\\n                if matrix[r][0] == 0 or matrix[0][c] == 0:\\n                    matrix[r][c] = 0\\n            if col0:\\n                matrix[r][0] = 0\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(m·n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Zeroing as you scan cascades zeros; apply markers bottom-up so row 0 is cleared last.",
