      "id": "nc150-happy-number",
      "front": "**Happy Number** · Easy\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/happy-number/)\\n\\nRepeatedly replace n with the sum of squares of its digits; decide whether it reaches 1.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Cycle detection (fast/slow)\\n\\n**Key insight:** The sequence either hits 1 or loops; Floyd's tortoise-and-hare detects it in O(1) space.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public boolean isHappy(int n) {\\n        int slow = n, fast = next(n);\\n        while (fast != 1 && slow != fast) {\\n            slow = next(slow);\\n            fast = next(next(fast));\\n        }\\n        return fast == 1;\\n    }\\n    int next(int n) {\\n        int s = 0;\\n        while (n > 0) { int d = n % 10; s += d * d; n /= 10; }\\n        return s;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def isHappy(self, n: int) -> bool:\\n        def nxt(x: int) -> int:\\n            return sum(int(d) ** 2 for d in str(x))\\n\\n        slow, fast = n, nxt(n)\\n        while fast != 1 and slow != fast:\\n            slow = nxt(slow)\\n            fast = nxt(nxt(fast))\\n        return fast == 1\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(log n) per step / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Looping until 1 without cycle detection never terminates for unhappy numbers.",
