      "front": "**Plus One** · Easy\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/plus-one/)\\n\\nAdd one to a big integer stored as an array of digits.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Carry from the right\\n\\n**Key insight:** Turn trailing 9s into 0; the first non-9 just increments. All 9s → new leading 1.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int[] plusOne(int[] digits) {\\n        for (int i = digits.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n            if (digits[i] < 9) { digits[i]++; return digits; }\\n            digits[i] = 0;\\n        }\\n        int[] res = new int[digits.length + 1];\\n        res[0] = 1;\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def plusOne(self, digits: List[int]) -> List[int]:\\n        for i in range(len(digits) - 1, -1, -1):\\n            if digits[i] < 9:\\n                digits[i] += 1\\n                return digits\\n            digits[i] = 0\\n        return [1] + digits\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1) (O(n) when all 9s)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Converting to a long overflows for long digit arrays.",
