      "front": "**Pow(x, n)** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/powx-n/)\\n\\nCompute x raised to an integer power n (n may be negative).\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Fast exponentiation (binary)\\n\\n**Key insight:** Square the base and halve the exponent; multiply into the result on odd bits.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public double myPow(double x, int n) {\\n        long e = n;\\n        if (e < 0) { x = 1 / x; e = -e; }\\n        double res = 1;\\n        while (e > 0) {\\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) res *= x;\\n            x *= x;\\n            e >>= 1;\\n        }\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def myPow(self, x: float, n: int) -> float:\\n        if n < 0:\\n            x, n = 1 / x, -n\\n        res = 1.0\\n        while n:\\n            if n & 1:\\n                res *= x\\n            x *= x\\n            n >>= 1\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(log n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Negating Integer.MIN_VALUE overflows in int — widen to long first.",
