      "id": "nc150-detect-squares",
      "front": "**Detect Squares** · Medium\\n\\n[LeetCode](https://leetcode.com/problems/detect-squares/)\\n\\nDesign a structure that adds points and counts axis-aligned squares formable with a query point.\\n\\nPattern? Approach?",
      "back": "**Pattern:** Hash counting over diagonal points\\n\\n**Key insight:** Treat each stored point as the diagonal corner; the other two corners are determined, so multiply their counts.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass DetectSquares {\\n    Map<Long, Integer> cnt = new HashMap<>();\\n    List<int[]> pts = new ArrayList<>();\\n    long key(int x, int y) { return ((long) x << 32) | (y & 0xffffffffL); }\\n    public DetectSquares() {}\\n    public void add(int[] p) {\\n        cnt.merge(key(p[0], p[1]), 1, Integer::sum);\\n        pts.add(p);\\n    }\\n    public int count(int[] p) {\\n        int res = 0;\\n        for (int[] d : pts) {\\n            if (Math.abs(d[0] - p[0]) != Math.abs(d[1] - p[1]) || d[0] == p[0]) continue;\\n            res += cnt.getOrDefault(key(p[0], d[1]), 0) * cnt.getOrDefault(key(d[0], p[1]), 0);\\n        }\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass DetectSquares:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.cnt = Counter()\\n        self.pts = []\\n\\n    def add(self, point: List[int]) -> None:\\n        self.cnt[tuple(point)] += 1\\n        self.pts.append(point)\\n\\n    def count(self, point: List[int]) -> int:\\n        px, py = point\\n        res = 0\\n        for x, y in self.pts:\\n            if abs(x - px) != abs(y - py) or x == px:\\n                continue\\n            res += self.cnt[(px, y)] * self.cnt[(x, py)]\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** add O(1), count O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Zero-area 'squares' (d equal to the query point) must be skipped; duplicates multiply.",
