      "back": "**Pattern:** XOR cancellation\\n\\n**Key insight:** x ^ x = 0 and XOR is commutative, so XOR of everything leaves the single.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int singleNumber(int[] nums) {\\n        int x = 0;\\n        for (int n : nums) x ^= n;\\n        return x;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom functools import reduce\\nfrom operator import xor\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def singleNumber(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\\n        return reduce(xor, nums, 0)\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** A HashSet works but violates the O(1)-space follow-up.",
