      "back": "**Pattern:** Clear lowest set bit\\n\\n**Key insight:** n & (n-1) drops the lowest 1, so loop once per set bit.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int hammingWeight(int n) {\\n        int c = 0;\\n        while (n != 0) { n &= n - 1; c++; }\\n        return c;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def hammingWeight(self, n: int) -> int:\\n        c = 0\\n        while n:\\n            n &= n - 1\\n            c += 1\\n        return c\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(set bits) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** With signed ints, use != 0 (not > 0) and >>> rather than >> if shifting.",
