      "back": "**Pattern:** DP on bits\\n\\n**Key insight:** bits[i] = bits[i >> 1] + (i & 1).\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int[] countBits(int n) {\\n        int[] res = new int[n + 1];\\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) res[i] = res[i >> 1] + (i & 1);\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def countBits(self, n: int) -> List[int]:\\n        res = [0] * (n + 1)\\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\\n            res[i] = res[i >> 1] + (i & 1)\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(n)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Calling a popcount per number is O(n log n) — fine, but misses the DP point.",
