      "back": "**Pattern:** Bit-by-bit shift\\n\\n**Key insight:** Shift result left, OR in n's lowest bit, shift n right (unsigned) — 32 times.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int reverseBits(int n) {\\n        int res = 0;\\n        for (int i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\\n            res = (res << 1) | (n & 1);\\n            n >>>= 1;\\n        }\\n        return res;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nclass Solution:\\n    def reverseBits(self, n: int) -> int:\\n        res = 0\\n        for _ in range(32):\\n            res = (res << 1) | (n & 1)\\n            n >>= 1\\n        return res\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(1) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Stopping when n hits 0 skips the trailing zeros that must become leading zeros.",
