      "back": "**Pattern:** XOR indices with values\\n\\n**Key insight:** XOR all indices 0..n with all values; pairs cancel and the missing number remains.\\n\\n**Java**\\n\\n\`\`\`java\\nclass Solution {\\n    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {\\n        int x = nums.length;\\n        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) x ^= i ^ nums[i];\\n        return x;\\n    }\\n}\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Python**\\n\\n\`\`\`python\\nfrom typing import List\\n\\nclass Solution:\\n    def missingNumber(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\\n        x = len(nums)\\n        for i, v in enumerate(nums):\\n            x ^= i ^ v\\n        return x\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)\\n\\n**Pitfall:** Forgetting to include n itself in the XOR (or in the expected sum).",
